meta {
  name: Widen Agent Scopes (POST /v1/agents/:registration_id/scopes)
  type: http
  seq: 168
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/agents/{{registrationId}}/scopes
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{sessionToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "scopes": ["atproto", "blob:*/*", "repo:*?action=create&action=update"]
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:8080
}

docs {
  # POST /v1/agents/{registration_id}/scopes

  The owner approves more of the operator's scope profile for a live agent (ADR-0041). `scopes`
  is the exact set the wallet's consent screen showed. The stored grant becomes
  `grant ∪ (scopes ∩ current profile)`: a shown scope outside the profile is never stored, and a
  stored scope the profile no longer allows is kept (suspended) and returns at the next renewal
  once the profile allows it again.

  Owner-authenticated (wallet session token or full-access access token); agent-derived and
  app-password credentials are refused. Accepts a `claimed` `identity_assertion`, `service_auth`,
  `anonymous` or `child` registration; a parent widens its children. The UPDATE and a
  `scopes_widened` audit event (`detail`: `before`, `shown`, `after`) commit together; a request
  that adds nothing writes neither.

  The agent picks the wider grant up at its next jwt-bearer renewal. For a dormant child, follow
  with `POST /agent/child/assertion` and hand the assertion over.

  ## Response (200)

  ```json
  {
    "scopes": ["atproto", "blob:*/*", "identity:*", "repo:*?action=create&action=update"],
    "effectiveScopes": ["atproto", "blob:*/*", "repo:*?action=create&action=update"]
  }
  ```

  `scopes` is the stored grant; `effectiveScopes` is it clamped to the current profile.

  ## Errors

  - 400 `InvalidRequest` — a `connector` / `oauth_app` grant (widen it through OAuth re-consent), or `scopes` missing
  - 403 `Forbidden` — the registration is not `claimed`
  - 404 `NotFound` — unknown, or another account's registration
  - 409 `Conflict` — the agent changed while the request was in flight; reload and retry
}
